y_caller":"Sean Payton"},{"season":2025,"team":"TEN","distance":0.8664,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Brian Callahan"}],"defense":[{"season":2024,"team":"LA","distance":0.1475,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Chris Shula"},{"season":2025,"team":"TEN","distance":0.2172,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennard Wilson"},{"season":2025,"team":"HOU","distance":0.2361,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Matt Burke"},{"season":2025,"team":"BAL","distance":0.2538,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"CIN","distance":0.2722,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Steelers are 6-2 through week 8 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 180 to 144. The defense has done most of the work, ranking 6th in EPA allowed while the offense sits 21st in EPA per play. Their most distinctive trait is the 2nd highest RPO rate in the league.","offense":"The Steelers offense has been a little below average by EPA per play so far, and it has been much better running the ball than passing it. They have thrown more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score has not called for it. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the 2nd highest RPO rate and the 2nd highest screen rate in the league. Aaron Rodgers has run the passing game, with DK Metcalf leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Steelers have one of the best defenses in the league this season, ranking 7th or better in three of the five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area has been sack rate, where it ranks 3rd, and it has no real weak spot. Alex Highsmith has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Nick Herbig, who has 3 sacks despite playing only 54% of the snaps. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a blitz rate that ranks 13th lowest in the league.","special":"The Steelers have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 78% of field goals, which is a little below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into linebackers, about 31% of the money on the books. Their linebackers were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Aaron Rodgers has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,871 yards. DK Metcalf has been the clear top target with 24% of the looks and 378 receiving yards. Jaylen Warren has handled most of the work in the backfield with 67% of the carries. On defense, T.J. Watt leads the team with 7.5 sacks.","coaching":"Mike McCarthy is calling the offense as head coach and Patrick Graham is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2024 Seahawks and the 2025 Chiefs under Andy Reid. Their defense looks most like the 2024 Rams under Chris Shula and the 2025 Titans under Dennard Wilson.","trends":"The offense went from 16th in EPA per play in 2025 to 21st so far this season, a modest decline. The defense moved from 18th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 6th so far this season, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was number of pass rushers, which went from 4.43 to 4.33.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}